Mid-afternoon slump, so I want something sweet and quick, and I'm not going to pretend I'm buying a fruit pot to feel virtuous. That warning label on the high-calorie stuff is a bit much, though it doesn't put me off, I'd just see the calorie badge and carry on.

I'll go for the Dairy Milk. It's what I'd actually want at 3pm.

{"choice": 5}

Oh, for goodness' sake, those gruesome pictures again. I'd have to squint past a bowel tumour just to get a packet of crisps, and I'm not looking at that while I'm waiting for a bit of pick-me-up.

I'd go for the McCoy's salt and vinegar. They're what I always end up reaching for, and the Doritos are too much for my blood pressure anyway.

{"choice": 3}

Honestly, mid-afternoon after a morning at the payroll desk, I'd want something I can eat with one hand and that won't leave me hungry before tea, so the Müller Corner gets the nod, though I'd have grumbled at the warning on the pot like it was the machine telling me off. Hmm, actually the Cadbury Dairy Milk would be my guilty pick if I'm being straight, because I'd rather have the chocolate than a fruit pot on a grey day.

Given I'm being completely honest about today, I'd buy the Dairy Milk.

{"choice": 10}
